      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 93, the garden strawberry kept as one entry (summer-fruiting and perpetual types share the care; the alpine strawberry is a separate species). Sources: NC State (current name page, the script's old address 404ed), RHS grow-your-own page (replant every three or four years, water new plants and dry spells, containers need regular watering, hardy; protect flowers from frost), ASPCA genus page (Fragaria spp., non-toxic to dogs and cats). NC State sizes 6 to 12 in by 1 to 2 ft; 30 by 60 cm is the agent's mapping. Light: NC State full sun to partial shade, full chosen. No Missouri BG or Clemson page found (search only). No RHS H rating read, so no hardiness. Pet toxicity rests on one genus-level source. Fruit is edible, so no child line; the leaves are not graded. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
